== helios (hidden false)
One small program that runs your machines.

Usage:
  helios [command]

Available Commands:
  alerts           What is wrong right now, and what was recently.
  backup           Back the app's data up to its bucket now. "helios" backs up the machine's own state.
  backups          List backups, drills and restores, newest first.
  capabilities     Print this build's supported contracts and read-only machine identity.
  check            Validate a manifest and its local source inputs without a host.
  cron             Hold a cron workload's scheduled runs for a while, or release the hold.
  daemon           The host daemon: run it, install it under systemd, or check it.
  deploy           Deploy the app in a source directory: build, start, check, switch the edge, retire the old revision.
  dns              The records behind every host this machine routes, as Cloudflare and the world see them.
  doctor           Check this machine and say what to fix. Changes nothing.
  drill            Prove a backup: restore it beside the app, start the app on it, check, clean up. Or skip the next scheduled one.
  edge             The edge in front of every app: which connections it takes.
  exec             Run a command inside a workload's container.
  exposure         What each container may do and what reaches it: user, capabilities, root filesystem, networks, ports, mounts.
  gc               Remove containers, images and build cache that no kept revision uses.
  git              Deploy by pushing: which keys may push which apps, remotes, and GitHub webhooks.
  history          List recent operations, show a receipt, or retrieve saved diagnostic output.
  host             Set up, keep and maintain this machine.
  init             Write a starting helios.yaml for a new app.
  integration      The credentials helios itself uses: storage for backups, email for alerts, Cloudflare for DNS.
  jobs             List recent cron runs and one-off commands.
  launch           Take a repository from nothing to running here.
  logs             Show a workload's output; the app's only workload when there is one.
  ls               List the apps on this machine: owner, hosts, repository, last deploy, last backup.
  move             Move an app, and its data, to another machine.
  peer             Other machines this one watches, and the ones allowed to read it. Kept sealed.
  preview          Run a branch of an app beside it, behind a sign-in.
  ps               List apps, their workloads and what is running.
  psql             Open psql on the app's database.
  recover          Recover an exact machine backup privately, or rehearse it in disposable isolation.
  rehearse         Test a candidate's releases and checks on an isolated restored backup.
  remove           Take an app off this machine. Its volumes, database and secrets stay unless asked.
  restore          Bring an app's data back from its bucket onto this machine, before deploying it here.
  rollback         Make the previous revision active again.
  run              Run a one-off command with a workload's image, environment, secrets and volumes.
  secret           Keep an app's secrets sealed on this machine.
  status           How the machine and its apps are doing: health, traffic, resources, backups, alerts.
  target           Configure explicit SSH targets with pinned host-key verification.
  upgrade          Replace helios with a new build and restart the daemon; systemd rolls back if it can't start.
  version          Print the version of this build.
  watch            Public URLs this machine checks from the outside, such as the other machine's sites.

Flags:
      --json                  print JSON, one object per line
      --socket string         the daemon's socket; the local kernel is used when nothing answers (default "/run/bedrock/bedrock.sock")
      --state-dir string      where helios keeps its state (default "~/.bedrock")
      --target string         operate on this explicitly named SSH target
      --targets-file string   the local named-target configuration (default "~/.bedrock/targets.json")

Use "helios [command] --help" for more information about a command.
