== helios check (hidden false)
Validate a manifest and its local source inputs without a host.
Validate a manifest and its local source inputs without a host.

Checks workload shapes, routes, ports and secret names with the deploy
validator, then checks build contexts, Dockerfiles, static directories
and PostgreSQL init inputs. Nothing is built or changed.

This is an offline check. It does not establish DNS, certificates,
image availability, secret values or capacity on a target machine.
Add --host while running on the target to check the same read-only
preconditions as helios deploy --plan, including integrations and
route/published-port ownership and availability of named secrets.
It does not execute the plan or prove disk/aggregate resource capacity,
runtime readiness, DNS or certificate issuance.
Usage:
  helios check [source-dir] [flags]

Flags:
      --host              also check deploy-plan preconditions on this target; applies and journals nothing
      --manifest string   the manifest at the source's root (default: helios.yaml, or bedrock.yaml)

Global Flags:
      --json                  print JSON, one object per line
      --socket string         the daemon's socket; the local kernel is used when nothing answers (default "/run/bedrock/bedrock.sock")
      --state-dir string      where helios keeps its state (default "~/.bedrock")
      --target string         operate on this explicitly named SSH target
      --targets-file string   the local named-target configuration (default "~/.bedrock/targets.json")
== helios cron (hidden false)
Hold a cron workload's scheduled runs for a while, or release the hold.

Usage:
  helios cron [command]

Available Commands:
  hold        Skip a cron workload's scheduled runs until a time, at most 14 days ahead, and say why. A run in progress finishes.
  release     End a cron workload's hold now. It runs again at its next scheduled time, with no catch-up run.

