== helios dns drop (hidden false)
Delete a record that points here for a host no app on this machine routes.
Delete a record that points here for a host no app on this machine routes,
such as one helios dns audit finds after an app was removed.

Only the A and AAAA records at exactly that name go, and only when every
record there points at this machine: a record that names another machine,
or a CNAME, refuses the drop. A wildcard that covers the host is never
touched; name the wildcard itself, such as '*.example.com', to drop it,
and only when no route here falls under it.
Usage:
  helios dns drop <host> [flags]

Flags:
      --digest string   apply only if the plan is still the one with this digest; implies --yes
      --plan            show the plan and change nothing
      --yes             apply without asking

Global Flags:
      --json                  print JSON, one object per line
      --socket string         the daemon's socket; the local kernel is used when nothing answers (default "/run/bedrock/bedrock.sock")
      --state-dir string      where helios keeps its state (default "~/.bedrock")
      --target string         operate on this explicitly named SSH target
      --targets-file string   the local named-target configuration (default "~/.bedrock/targets.json")
