== helios edge origin-pull (hidden false)
Have a host behind Cloudflare's proxy take only the connections Cloudflare makes.
Have a host behind Cloudflare's proxy take only the connections Cloudflare makes.

Cloudflare presents a client certificate on every connection it makes to
the host, and the edge takes only those a CA it trusts for the host signed,
so knowing the machine's address gets nobody past Cloudflare.

  helios edge origin-pull mint shop.example.com --out shop.pem

Upload the file at Cloudflare as a per-hostname authenticated origin pull
certificate for the host, with the zone's SSL/TLS mode at Full (strict).
Deploy with origin_pull: optional on the host's routes, check that requests
through Cloudflare still succeed, then deploy with origin_pull: required.
Usage:
  helios edge origin-pull [command]

Available Commands:
  forget      Stop trusting one of a host's CAs, or all of them; refused if a host that requires origin pull would be left with none.
  list        List the hosts that use origin pull, their mode, and the CAs they trust until when.
  mint        Make the certificate Cloudflare presents for a host, trust its CA, and write the certificate and its key to a new file.
  trust       Trust a CA's certificate for a host, from a file or stdin, as on a machine taking a host over.

Global Flags:
      --json                  print JSON, one object per line
      --socket string         the daemon's socket; the local kernel is used when nothing answers (default "/run/bedrock/bedrock.sock")
      --state-dir string      where helios keeps its state (default "~/.bedrock")
      --target string         operate on this explicitly named SSH target
      --targets-file string   the local named-target configuration (default "~/.bedrock/targets.json")

Use "helios edge origin-pull [command] --help" for more information about a command.
