== helios git require-signed (hidden false)
Deploy an app only from commits an allowed signer signed, over push and webhook; --off deploys any commit again.
Deploy an app only from commits an allowed signer signed, over push and webhook.

The commit that deploys, the tip of the push or of the branch a webhook
names, must carry an SSH signature by a key helios git signers allows.
An unsigned tip, a key nobody allowed, a GPG signature (GitHub's on the
merges it makes among them) or a key not allowed to sign git commits is
refused, and nothing of it is built. A tree uploaded with helios deploy
--to bedrock@ is refused too, since it has no commit to check; root can
still deploy one, with helios deploy on the machine or --to root@.

To sign, on the machine you commit from:

  git config gpg.format ssh
  git config user.signingkey ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
  git config commit.gpgsign true

Allow the signer first, then require signatures:

  helios git signers add kyle@example.com "$(cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub)"
  helios git require-signed hello
Usage:
  helios git require-signed <app> [flags]

Flags:
      --digest string   apply only if the plan is still the one with this digest; implies --yes
      --off             deploy the app from any commit again, signed or not
      --plan            show the plan and change nothing
      --yes             apply without asking

Global Flags:
      --json                  print JSON, one object per line
      --socket string         the daemon's socket; the local kernel is used when nothing answers (default "/run/bedrock/bedrock.sock")
      --state-dir string      where helios keeps its state (default "~/.bedrock")
      --target string         operate on this explicitly named SSH target
      --targets-file string   the local named-target configuration (default "~/.bedrock/targets.json")
