== helios history (hidden false)
List recent operations, show a receipt, or retrieve saved diagnostic output.
List recent operations, show a receipt, or retrieve saved diagnostic output.

List filters are combined and applied before --limit. --failed includes
failed and compensated operations. --since accepts a positive duration
such as 24h, or an RFC3339 timestamp such as 2026-10-10T12:00:00Z.

  helios history --app api --kind app.deploy --failed --since 24h
  helios history <operation-id> --output
  helios history <operation-id> --output --step build-web

Output is opt-in and contains saved tails, not a complete log. Each step
execution keeps up to 40 lines; a running execution's output is saved when
it finishes. --step selects an exact name or a one-based step position.
Usage:
  helios history [operation-id] [flags]

Flags:
      --app string     only operations targeting this app
      --failed         only failed or compensated operations
      --kind string    only this operation kind, such as app.deploy
      --limit int      how many matching operations to list (default 20)
      --output         show the operation's saved step-output tails instead of its receipt
      --since string   operations created since a duration ago or an RFC3339 timestamp
      --step string    with --output, select a step by name or one-based position

Global Flags:
      --json                  print JSON, one object per line
      --socket string         the daemon's socket; the local kernel is used when nothing answers (default "/run/bedrock/bedrock.sock")
      --state-dir string      where helios keeps its state (default "~/.bedrock")
