== helios move resume (hidden false)
Deliberately resume a frozen source after stopping the target.
Deliberately resume a frozen source after stopping the target.

--target-stopped records your assertion that no destination writers remain.
The source cannot prove this across disconnected machines. Its data excludes
changes made on the destination; use a reverse move to preserve those writes.
Resume does not change DNS. Review DNS separately before returning traffic.
Usage:
  helios move resume <app> [flags]

Flags:
      --digest string    apply only if the plan is still the one with this digest; implies --yes
      --plan             show the plan and change nothing
      --target-stopped   confirm that destination writers have been stopped; source data excludes destination writes
      --yes              apply without asking

