== helios preview (hidden false)
Run a branch of an app beside it, behind a sign-in.
Run a branch of an app beside it, behind a sign-in.

A preview is an ordinary app with a derived name, its own containers and its
own empty database, deployed from a branch. Pushing the same branch again
updates it rather than making a second one.

  helios preview up https://github.com/you/app --branch new-nav \
      --domain preview.example.com
  helios preview ls
  helios preview down app --branch new-nav
  helios preview pin app --branch new-nav
  helios preview prune --older-than 7d --plan

Every preview route is behind the Core's sign-in and there is no way to turn
that off, so the machine needs the loom integration before any of this works.
Usage:
  helios preview [command]

Available Commands:
  down        Remove a preview, including its data and secrets.
  ls          List the previews running on this machine.
  pin         Keep a preview out of preview prune.
  prune       Remove old, unpinned previews with one reviewable plan.
  unpin       Allow preview prune to remove this preview when old enough.
  up          Deploy a branch as a preview of the app in it.

Global Flags:
      --json                  print JSON, one object per line
      --socket string         the daemon's socket; the local kernel is used when nothing answers (default "/run/bedrock/bedrock.sock")
      --state-dir string      where helios keeps its state (default "~/.bedrock")
      --target string         operate on this explicitly named SSH target
      --targets-file string   the local named-target configuration (default "~/.bedrock/targets.json")

Use "helios preview [command] --help" for more information about a command.
