== helios remove (hidden false)
Take an app off this machine. Its volumes, database and secrets stay unless asked.
Take an app off this machine. Its volumes, database and sealed secrets
stay unless asked, so it can be restored or deployed again with what it had.

--data removes them too, the secrets included. For an app that is no longer
on this machine, --data removes whatever it left behind: its sealed secrets,
volumes, database and networks. Its backups in the storage bucket stay, and
are the only way back.
Usage:
  helios remove <app> [flags]

Flags:
      --data            also remove the app's volumes, database and sealed secrets, or what a removed app left; only a backup brings them back
      --digest string   apply only if the plan is still the one with this digest; implies --yes
      --plan            show the plan and change nothing
      --secrets         also forget the app's sealed secrets, keeping its volumes and database
      --yes             apply without asking

Global Flags:
      --json                  print JSON, one object per line
      --socket string         the daemon's socket; the local kernel is used when nothing answers (default "/run/bedrock/bedrock.sock")
      --state-dir string      where helios keeps its state (default "~/.bedrock")
      --target string         operate on this explicitly named SSH target
      --targets-file string   the local named-target configuration (default "~/.bedrock/targets.json")
