== helios upgrade (hidden false)
Replace helios with a new build and restart the daemon; systemd rolls back if it can't start.
Replace helios with a new build and restart the daemon; systemd rolls back if it can't start.

With --version the build is downloaded from the published release and checked
against the SHA256SUMS beside it, which counts only when a Helios release key
pinned in this build signed it. A release without that signature is refused.
Pass --sha256 with a checksum from reviewed source to pin the build instead;
that also installs a release from before releases were signed.

  helios upgrade --version 0.7.15
  helios upgrade --version 0.7.14 --sha256 <checksum>
  helios upgrade /tmp/helios-new
Usage:
  helios upgrade [path-to-new-helios] [flags]

Flags:
      --digest string    apply only if the plan is still the one with this digest; implies --yes
      --plan             show the plan and change nothing
      --sha256 string    the expected checksum of that release's build for this machine
      --version string   a published release to fetch and install, such as 0.7.4
      --yes              apply without asking

Global Flags:
      --json                  print JSON, one object per line
      --socket string         the daemon's socket; the local kernel is used when nothing answers (default "/run/bedrock/bedrock.sock")
      --state-dir string      where helios keeps its state (default "~/.bedrock")
      --target string         operate on this explicitly named SSH target
      --targets-file string   the local named-target configuration (default "~/.bedrock/targets.json")
